+Federated Learning (FL) scaffold for Aegis
+
+This scaffold provides lightweight, auditable building blocks to add federated learning capability to Aegis:
+- FL server (round controller) with REST endpoints for client register / get_round / submit_update
+- FL client SDK (lightweight) that fetches global model, performs local update (simulated), signs update bundle and uploads
+- Aggregation algorithms: FedAvg, FedProx, Krum (robust aggregator) and median
+- Secure aggregation / DP stubs (placeholders): integrate Opacus or secure aggregation later
+- Client attestation and identity stubs (cert/csr / TPM/SGX placeholders)
+- Evidence & provenance integration: signed client update bundles; uses ADK evidence bundler and cosign hooks
+- Validator worker that replays aggregated model on holdout data and produces quality checks
+- K8s manifests: FL server deployment and client Job template + RBAC
+- CI workflow to run simulated FL rounds and validation with signing + Rekor verification
+
+NOTES:
+- This is a scaffold. Replace simulated training with your local training loop, integrate Opacus or secure aggregation library,
+  and wire attestation and private key provisioning to Vault/TPM or cloud KMS before production use.
+
